      "worked": "Require $\\cos x\\ne0$. Use $\\sec^2x=1+\\tan^2x$ and the index laws.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}3\\cdot3^{\\tan^2x}+3^{\\tan^2x}&=12\\\\4\\cdot3^{\\tan^2x}&=12\\\\3^{\\tan^2x}&=3\\\\\\tan^2x&=1\\\\\\tan x&=\\pm1\\\\x&=\\frac{\\pi}{4},\\frac{3\\pi}{4},\\frac{5\\pi}{4},\\frac{7\\pi}{4}\\end{align*}$$\n\nAll four angles have nonzero cosine. At each, $\\tan^2x=1$ and $\\sec^2x=2$, so the original left-hand side is $3^2+3^1=12$.",
